/-!
# The short-root type-G2 carrier over the prime field of characteristic three

The short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `ℤ` is the Kostant toral closure of the seven-dimensional
module `V(ϖ₁)` inside `GL₇`: the largest Hopf ideal of `O(GL₇/ℤ)` killed by the coordinate maps of
the four numbered simple root subgroups and of the rank-two weight torus. This file forms the
companion carrier over the prime field `𝔽₃`: the closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇` over `𝔽₃`
generated by the reductions of those same coordinate maps.

Over `𝔽₃` the defining ideal is again maximal among Hopf ideals killed by the generators, this
time by construction. That maximality is what lets a homomorphism to `GL₇` satisfying the
generator equations be restricted to an endomorphism of the carrier, and it is not available for
the base change of the integral carrier, whose defining ideal is maximal over `ℤ` only: new
equations can appear over a base that is not flat. The two carriers are compared in the honest
direction only, and no flatness is asserted.

The root subgroups, the weight torus, and the pinning equations are the reductions of the
integral ones, so nothing about the matrices is re-derived: the point homomorphisms below have
the same matrices as the integral carrier's, and every equation between those matrices transfers.

The carrier is not identified with the pinned simply connected group scheme of type `G₂`, and
constructions on it transfer to that group scheme only along such an identification, once one is
proved.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.generator`: the reduced coordinate maps of the four numbered
  simple root subgroups and of the weight torus.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.groupScheme`: the closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇` over `𝔽₃`
  they generate, with `carrierι` its closed immersion into `GL₇`.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.rootSubgroup` and
  `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.weightTorus`: the generators, factored through it.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.points`: its matrix-valued points over an `𝔽₃`-algebra, with
  `rootSubgroupPoints` and `weightTorusPoints` the pinned subgroups of those points, and
  `pointsMap` their functoriality in the value algebra.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.frobenius`: the `3 ^ m`-power Frobenius endomorphism of those
  points.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.coe_rootSubgroupPoints` and
  `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.coe_weightTorusPoints`: the pinned points have the matrices of
  the integral carrier's pinned points, namely `1 + t X + t² Y` and the weight-diagonal matrix.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.baseChangePresentationIdeal_le_definingIdeal` and
  `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.points_le_baseChangePresentationPoints`: the carrier over `𝔽₃`
  is a closed subgroup scheme of the base change of the integral carrier, and its points lie in
  the points of that base change.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.weightTorusPoints_conj_rootSubgroupPoints`: the pinning
  equation on matrix-valued points.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.frobenius_zero` and
  `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.frobenius_add`: the Frobenius iterates start at the identity and
  add under composition.
* `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.frobenius_rootSubgroupPoints` and
  `TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.PrimeField.frobenius_weightTorusPoints`: the Frobenius raises the
  parameter of a numbered simple root subgroup, and every torus coordinate, to its `3 ^ m`-th
  power.

## References

The construction is the Chevalley--Demazure construction on the seven-dimensional module, formed
over the prime field; see R. W. Carter, *Simple Groups of Lie Type*, §§4.4 and 7.1, and
J. E. Humphreys, *Linear Algebraic Groups*, §26. The weight conventions follow N. Bourbaki, *Lie
Groups and Lie Algebras, Chapters 4--6*, Plate IX.
-/

public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

namespace TauCeti.G2ShortRoot

open TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing
attribute [local instance high] Algebra.toModule

universe v

local notation "CM" => CartanMatrix.G₂
local notation "rootGen" => TauCeti.serreRootGenerator CM
local notation "cartanGen" => TauCeti.serreH ℚ CM
local notation "rootWeight" => DynkinType.G2.rootGeneratorWeight DynkinType.valid_G2

namespace PrimeField

/-- The coordinate Hopf algebra receiving a reduced root-subgroup or weight-torus generator: that
of the additive group over `𝔽₃` at a root index, and that of the rank-two split torus over `𝔽₃`
at the torus index. -/
noncomputable abbrev generatorCodomain :
    (Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) ⊕ Unit → CommHopfAlgCat (ZMod 3)
  | .inl _ => AdditiveGroup.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3)
  | .inr _ => (DiagonalizableGroup.coordinateRing (ZMod 3)
      (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))).obj

/-- The generating coordinate maps of the short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃`: the reductions
of the four numbered simple root-subgroup coordinate maps and of the weight-torus coordinate map,
transported into the coordinate Hopf algebras formed directly over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def generator :
    ∀ j, TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7 ⟶ generatorCodomain j
  | .inl k => kostantRootSubgroupBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen rep
      lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
      isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis (ZMod 3) k
  | .inr _ => TauCeti.GeneralLinear.weightTorusBaseChangeCoordinateMap ℤ (ZMod 3) weight

/-- At a root index the generating family is the reduced root-subgroup coordinate map. -/
theorem generator_inl (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    generator (.inl k) =
      kostantRootSubgroupBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen rep
        lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
        isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis (ZMod 3) k := by
  rw [generator]

/-- At the torus index the generating family is the reduced weight-torus coordinate map. -/
theorem generator_inr :
    generator (.inr ()) =
      TauCeti.GeneralLinear.weightTorusBaseChangeCoordinateMap ℤ (ZMod 3) weight := by
  rw [generator]

/-- The Hopf ideal cutting out the short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃` inside `GL₇`: the
largest Hopf ideal of `O(GL₇/𝔽₃)` killed by all the reduced generators. -/
noncomputable def definingIdeal :
    HopfIdeal (ZMod 3) (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7) :=
  CommHopfAlgCat.commonKernelHopfIdeal generator

/-- The defining ideal is the common-kernel ideal of the reduced generators. -/
theorem definingIdeal_def :
    definingIdeal = CommHopfAlgCat.commonKernelHopfIdeal generator := by
  rw [definingIdeal]

/-- **The short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃`**: the closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇` over `𝔽₃`
generated by the reductions of the numbered simple root subgroups and of the weight torus. -/
noncomputable abbrev groupScheme : Grp (Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of (ZMod 3)))) :=
  TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupScheme 7 generator

/-- The quotient-spectrum presentation of the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
theorem groupScheme_def :
    groupScheme = CommHopfAlgCat.quotientSpec
      (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7) definingIdeal := by
  rw [groupScheme, definingIdeal]

/-- The canonical inclusion of the carrier over `𝔽₃` into `GL₇`. -/
noncomputable def carrierι : groupScheme ⟶ TauCeti.GeneralLinear.groupScheme (ZMod 3) 7 :=
  TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeι 7 generator

/-- The ambient inclusion is the one of the generated subgroup scheme. -/
theorem carrierι_def :
    carrierι = TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeι 7 generator := by
  rw [carrierι]

/-- The carrier over `𝔽₃` is a closed subgroup scheme of `GL₇`. -/
instance isClosedImmersion_carrierι : IsClosedImmersion carrierι.hom.hom.left := by
  rw [carrierι]
  exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.isClosedImmersion_generatedGroupSchemeι 7 generator

/-- A positive or negative numbered simple root subgroup of the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def rootSubgroup (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    AdditiveGroup.groupScheme (ZMod 3) ⟶ groupScheme :=
  eqToHom (AdditiveGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)) ≫
    TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeGenerator 7 generator (.inl k)

/-- The numbered root subgroup is the generator of the generated subgroup scheme it indexes. -/
theorem rootSubgroup_def (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) :
    rootSubgroup k =
      eqToHom (AdditiveGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3)) ≫
        TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeGenerator 7 generator (.inl k) := by
  rw [rootSubgroup]

/-- The rank-two split weight torus in the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def weightTorus : SplitTorus.groupScheme (ZMod 3) (Fin 2) ⟶ groupScheme :=
  eqToHom (DiagonalizableGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))) ≫
    TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeGenerator 7 generator (.inr ())

/-- The weight torus is the generator of the generated subgroup scheme it indexes. -/
theorem weightTorus_def :
    weightTorus =
      eqToHom
          (DiagonalizableGroup.groupScheme_def (ZMod 3) (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))) ≫
        TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedGroupSchemeGenerator 7 generator (.inr ()) := by
  rw [weightTorus]

/-- **The carrier over `𝔽₃` is a closed subgroup scheme of the base change of the integral
short-root carrier.** The reverse containment is not claimed: the integral defining ideal is the
largest Hopf ideal killed by the generators over `ℤ` only, and new equations can appear over a
base that is not flat. -/
theorem baseChangePresentationIdeal_le_definingIdeal :
    kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup
        rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight
        (ZMod 3) ≤
      definingIdeal := by
  rw [definingIdeal_def, CommHopfAlgCat.le_commonKernelHopfIdeal_iff]
  rintro (k | ⟨⟩)
  · rw [generator_inl]
    exact kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal_toIdeal_le_root_ker rootGen cartanGen rep
      lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator
      latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3) k
  · rw [generator_inr]
    exact kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal_toIdeal_le_torus_ker rootGen cartanGen rep
      lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator
      latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3)

/-! ## Matrix-valued points -/

/-- The matrix-valued points of the short-root type-`G₂` carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def points (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] :
    Subgroup (_root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) :=
  TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedPointsSubgroup 7 generator A

/-- The points of the carrier over `𝔽₃` are the points of the subgroup scheme generated by the
reduced generators. -/
theorem points_def (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] :
    points A = TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedPointsSubgroup 7 generator A := by
  rw [points]

/-- The points of the carrier over `𝔽₃` are cut out by its defining Hopf ideal. -/
theorem points_eq_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] :
    points A = TauCeti.GeneralLinear.hopfIdealPointsSubgroup 7 definingIdeal A := by
  rw [points, definingIdeal]
  exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.generatedPointsSubgroup_def 7 generator A

/-- A matrix is a point of the carrier over `𝔽₃` exactly when its associated convolution point
kills the carrier's defining Hopf ideal. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_points_iff (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    (g : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) :
    g ∈ points A ↔ ∀ x ∈ definingIdeal,
      ((TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) 7).symm g).ofConv x = 0 := by
  rw [points_eq_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup]
  exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.mem_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup_iff 7 definingIdeal A g

/-- **Every point of the carrier over `𝔽₃` is a point of the base change of the integral
short-root carrier.** -/
theorem points_le_baseChangePresentationPoints (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] :
    points A ≤ TauCeti.GeneralLinear.hopfIdealPointsSubgroup 7
      (kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup
        rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight
        (ZMod 3)) A := by
  rw [points_eq_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup]
  exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.hopfIdealPointsSubgroup_le_of_le 7
    baseChangePresentationIdeal_le_definingIdeal A

/-- The parametrized numbered simple root subgroup inside the points of the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def rootSubgroupPoints (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) (A : Type v) [CommRing A]
    [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] : Multiplicative A →* points A :=
  MonoidHom.codRestrict
    (((TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) 7).toMonoidHom.comp
        ((CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor (generator (.inl k))).app
          (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)).hom).comp
      (AdditiveGroup.gaPointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) (A := A)).symm.toMonoidHom)
    (points A)
    fun _ => TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv_mapPointsFunctor_mem_generatedPointsSubgroup
      7 generator (.inl k) A _

/-- **A numbered simple-root point of the carrier over `𝔽₃` is the corresponding point of the
integral carrier**, as a matrix. -/
theorem coe_rootSubgroupPoints (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) (A : Type v) [CommRing A]
    [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] (u : Multiplicative A) :
    (rootSubgroupPoints k A u : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) =
      (_root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.rootSubgroupPoints k A u :
        _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) := by
  set q : HopfAlgebra.points (R := ZMod 3)
      (H := AdditiveGroup.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3)) (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) :=
    (AdditiveGroup.gaPointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) (A := A)).symm u with hqdef
  have hu : AdditiveGroup.gaPointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) (A := A) q = u := by
    rw [hqdef, MulEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  have hq := pointsMulEquiv_kostantRootSubgroupToralBaseChangeCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen
    rep lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator
    latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3) _root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.definingIdeal_def k
    (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q
  rw [hu] at hq
  have hcomp :
      (CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor (generator (.inl k))).app (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q =
        CommHopfAlgCat.quotientPointsHom
          (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7)
          (kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup
            rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight
            (ZMod 3))
          (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)
          ((CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor
            (kostantRootSubgroupToralBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen rep
              lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
              isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3) k)).app
            (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q) := by
    rw [CommHopfAlgCat.quotientPointsHom, generator_inl,
      ← mkQuotient_comp_kostantRootSubgroupToralBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap
        rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
        isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3) k,
      CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor_comp]
    rfl
  rw [coe_rootSubgroupPoints_eq_kostantRootSubgroupMatrix, ← hq, ← hcomp]
  rfl

/-- A numbered simple-root point of the carrier over `𝔽₃` is the image of the corresponding point
of `𝔾ₐ` under the generating coordinate map. -/
theorem coe_rootSubgroupPoints_gaPointsMulEquiv (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) (A : Type v) [CommRing A]
    [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    (q : HopfAlgebra.points (R := ZMod 3)
      (H := AdditiveGroup.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3)) (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)) :
    (rootSubgroupPoints k A (AdditiveGroup.gaPointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) q) :
        _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) =
      TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv 7
        ((CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor (generator (.inl k))).app
          (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q) := by
  rw [rootSubgroupPoints]
  exact congrArg _ (congrArg _ (MulEquiv.symm_apply_apply _ q))

/-- The split weight torus inside the points of the carrier over `𝔽₃`. -/
noncomputable def weightTorusPoints (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] :
    (Fin 2 → Aˣ) →* points A :=
  MonoidHom.codRestrict
    (((TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) 7).toMonoidHom.comp
        ((CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor (generator (.inr ()))).app
          (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)).hom).comp
      (SplitTorus.pointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) (A := CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)
        (σ := Fin 2)).symm.toMonoidHom)
    (points A)
    fun _ => TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv_mapPointsFunctor_mem_generatedPointsSubgroup
      7 generator (.inr ()) A _

/-- **A weight-torus point of the carrier over `𝔽₃` is the corresponding point of the integral
carrier**, as a matrix. -/
theorem coe_weightTorusPoints (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] (s : Fin 2 → Aˣ) :
    (weightTorusPoints A s : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) =
      (_root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.weightTorusPoints A s :
        _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) := by
  set q : HopfAlgebra.points (R := ZMod 3)
      (H := (DiagonalizableGroup.coordinateRing (ZMod 3)
        (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))).obj) (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) :=
    (SplitTorus.pointsMulEquiv (R := ZMod 3) (A := CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)
      (σ := Fin 2)).symm s with hqdef
  have hs : SplitTorus.pointsMulEquiv q = s := by
    rw [hqdef, MulEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  have hq := pointsMulEquiv_kostantWeightTorusToralBaseChangeCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen
    rep lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator
    latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3) _root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.definingIdeal_def
    (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q
  rw [hs] at hq
  have hcomp :
      (CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor (generator (.inr ()))).app (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q =
        CommHopfAlgCat.quotientPointsHom
          (TauCeti.GeneralLinear.coordinateHopfAlgebra (ZMod 3) 7)
          (kostantToralBaseChangePresentationIdeal rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup
            rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight
            (ZMod 3))
          (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)
          ((CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor
            (kostantWeightTorusToralBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap rootGen cartanGen rep
              lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
              isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3))).app
            (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q) := by
    rw [CommHopfAlgCat.quotientPointsHom, generator_inr,
      ← mkQuotient_comp_kostantWeightTorusToralBaseChangePresentationCoordinateMap
        rootGen cartanGen rep lattice.toAddSubgroup rep_kostantForm_mem_lattice
        isNilpotent_rep_serreRootGenerator latticeBasis weight (ZMod 3),
      CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor_comp]
    rfl
  rw [_root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.coe_weightTorusPoints, ← hq, ← hcomp]
  rfl

/-- A weight-torus point of the carrier over `𝔽₃` is the image of the corresponding point of the
split torus under the generating coordinate map. -/
theorem coe_weightTorusPoints_pointsMulEquiv (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    (q : HopfAlgebra.points (R := ZMod 3)
      (H := (DiagonalizableGroup.coordinateRing (ZMod 3)
        (SplitTorus.characterGroup (Fin 2))).obj) (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A)) :
    (weightTorusPoints A (SplitTorus.pointsMulEquiv q) :
        _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) =
      TauCeti.GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv 7
        ((CommHopfAlgCat.mapPointsFunctor (generator (.inr ()))).app
          (CommAlgCat.of (ZMod 3) A) q) := by
  rw [weightTorusPoints]
  exact congrArg _ (congrArg _ (MulEquiv.symm_apply_apply _ q))

/-- **The pinning equation on matrix-valued points of the carrier over `𝔽₃`**: conjugation by a
point `s` of the weight torus rescales the parameter of each numbered simple root subgroup by the
corresponding type-`G₂` root character evaluated at `s`. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightTorusPoints_conj_rootSubgroupPoints (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) (A : Type v) [CommRing A]
    [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] (s : Fin 2 → Aˣ) (u : Multiplicative A) :
    weightTorusPoints A s * rootSubgroupPoints k A u * (weightTorusPoints A s)⁻¹ =
      rootSubgroupPoints k A
        (Multiplicative.ofAdd
          ((TauCeti.torusCharacter s (rootWeight k) : A) * Multiplicative.toAdd u)) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  have hint := congrArg Subtype.val
    (_root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.weightTorusPoints_conj_rootSubgroupPoints k A s u)
  simpa only [Subgroup.coe_mul, Subgroup.coe_inv, coe_weightTorusPoints,
    coe_rootSubgroupPoints] using hint

/-! ## Functoriality and the Frobenius -/

/-- The map on the points of the carrier over `𝔽₃` induced by a homomorphism of `𝔽₃`-algebras. -/
noncomputable def pointsMap {A B : Type v} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    [Algebra (ZMod 3) B] (f : A →ₐ[ZMod 3] B) : points A →* points B :=
  MonoidHom.codRestrict
    ((_root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.map (f : A →+* B)).comp (points A).subtype)
    (points B) fun g => by
      rw [points_eq_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup]
      exact TauCeti.GeneralLinear.map_mem_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup 7 definingIdeal f
        (by rw [← points_eq_hopfIdealPointsSubgroup]; exact g.2)

/-- The induced map on points applies the algebra homomorphism entrywise. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_pointsMap {A B : Type v} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    [Algebra (ZMod 3) B] (f : A →ₐ[ZMod 3] B) (g : points A) :
    (pointsMap f g : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) B) =
      _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.map (f : A →+* B) g := by
  rw [pointsMap]
  rfl

/-- **The `3 ^ m`-power Frobenius endomorphism of the carrier over `𝔽₃`**, the map on points
induced by the iterated Frobenius of the value algebra.

For `m` positive and `A` an algebraic closure of `𝔽₃`, this is the `3 ^ m`-power Frobenius of the
carrier's points; at `m = 0` it is the identity. -/
noncomputable def frobenius (m : ℕ) (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    [ExpChar A 3] : points A →* points A :=
  pointsMap (TauCeti.iterateFrobeniusAlgHom 3 m A)

/-- The Frobenius endomorphism of the carrier over `𝔽₃` acts by the entrywise Frobenius. -/
theorem coe_frobenius (m : ℕ) (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] [ExpChar A 3]
    (g : points A) :
    (frobenius m A g : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) =
      _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.map (iterateFrobenius A 3 m) g := by
  rw [frobenius, coe_pointsMap, TauCeti.coe_iterateFrobeniusAlgHom]

/-- Entrywise, the Frobenius endomorphism of the carrier over `𝔽₃` raises each matrix coefficient
to its `3 ^ m`-th power. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_frobenius_apply (m : ℕ) (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] [ExpChar A 3]
    (g : points A) (i j : Fin 7) :
    ((frobenius m A g : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) :
        Matrix (Fin 7) (Fin 7) A) i j =
      ((g : _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin 7) A) :
        Matrix (Fin 7) (Fin 7) A) i j ^ 3 ^ m := by
  rw [coe_frobenius, _root_.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.map_apply, iterateFrobenius_def]

/-- The zeroth Frobenius iterate is the identity on the carrier's point group. -/
@[simp]
theorem frobenius_zero (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] [ExpChar A 3] :
    frobenius 0 A = MonoidHom.id _ := by
  refine MonoidHom.ext fun g => ?_
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply _root_.Units.ext
  ext a b
  rw [coe_frobenius_apply]
  simp

/-- Frobenius iterates add under composition on the carrier's point group. -/
theorem frobenius_add (m k : ℕ) (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A] [ExpChar A 3] :
    frobenius (m + k) A = (frobenius m A).comp (frobenius k A) := by
  refine MonoidHom.ext fun g => ?_
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply _root_.Units.ext
  ext a b
  rw [coe_frobenius_apply, MonoidHom.comp_apply, coe_frobenius_apply, coe_frobenius_apply,
    ← pow_mul, ← pow_add, Nat.add_comm k m]

/-- **Frobenius raises the parameter of every numbered simple root subgroup to its `3 ^ m`-th
power.** -/
@[simp]
theorem frobenius_rootSubgroupPoints (m : ℕ) (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    [ExpChar A 3] (k : Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 2) (u : Multiplicative A) :
    frobenius m A (rootSubgroupPoints k A u) =
      rootSubgroupPoints k A (Multiplicative.ofAdd (Multiplicative.toAdd u ^ 3 ^ m)) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_frobenius, coe_rootSubgroupPoints, coe_rootSubgroupPoints,
    ← _root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.coe_pointsMap (iterateFrobenius A 3 m),
    _root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.pointsMap_rootSubgroupPoints]
  rfl

/-- **Frobenius raises every coordinate of the pinned split weight torus to its `3 ^ m`-th
power.** -/
@[simp]
theorem frobenius_weightTorusPoints (m : ℕ) (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra (ZMod 3) A]
    [ExpChar A 3] (s : Fin 2 → Aˣ) :
    frobenius m A (weightTorusPoints A s) = weightTorusPoints A (s ^ 3 ^ m) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [coe_frobenius, coe_weightTorusPoints, coe_weightTorusPoints,
    ← _root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.coe_pointsMap (iterateFrobenius A 3 m),
    _root_.TauCeti.G2ShortRoot.pointsMap_weightTorusPoints,
    _root_.TauCeti.map_iterateFrobenius_units_eq_pow]

end PrimeField

